{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":287742,"duration_api_ms":282048,"num_turns":47,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"63208a9b-8aaf-4b96-b3a7-3a582a435cd6","total_cost_usd":2.2189577500000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":42,"cache_creation_input_tokens":81065,"cache_read_input_tokens":2981933,"output_tokens":8845,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":81065,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":42,"outputTokens":8845,"cacheReadInputTokens":2981933,"cacheCreationInputTokens":81065,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.2189577500000004,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Reviewed the full diff (15 files, ~1000 insertions). The changes span: (1) molt cycle refactoring with per-stage resolution, multiplicative success scoring, new condition/reserve modifiers, and critical GH deficit gate; (2) invariant validation for new shrimp params; (3) save schema migration v12→v13; (4) snapshot field removal; (5) extensive test rewrites. The geometry-scaling infrastructure (filter flow, heater sizing, plant biomass, auto-stocking) was already in place from prior work — this diff focuses on the molt/mineral system refinements. Code compiles and all tests pass. Found two correctness/robustness concerns and one minor inconsistency.","amendments":[{"body":"In `update_molt_stress` (shrimp.rs:356), `(params.gh_min_d - gh_d) / params.gh_min_d` divides by `gh_min_d` without a `.max(0.01)` guard. Although invariant validation allows `gh_min_d == 0.0` via `check_non_negative`, making the branch unreachable in practice (since `gh_d < 0.0` cannot happen), the sister function `gh_mineral_factor` (line 1232) retains the `.max(0.01)` guard while `molt_mineral_modifier` (line 1247) does not. Either tighten the invariant to `check_positive` for `gh_min_d`, or add matching `.max(f64::EPSILON)` guards in `molt_mineral_modifier` and `update_molt_stress` for defensive consistency.","rationale":"The inconsistency between `gh_mineral_factor` (guarded) and `molt_mineral_modifier`/`update_molt_stress` (unguarded) for `gh_min_d` division creates a latent division-by-zero risk if invariant validation is ever relaxed or bypassed (e.g., during test setup). Both paths should use the same defensive strategy."},{"body":"In `molt_cycle`, `failed_molt_accum` now scales with `failed_stage_count` (up to 3), meaning a single-day resolution can add up to 0.9 (was capped at 0.3). Similarly, recovery scales with `successful_stage_count` (up to 1.05 recovery in one day). This amplification is not documented as an intentional design change and may cause unexpectedly rapid population decline when all three life stages fail simultaneously. Add a brief doc-comment on the scaling rationale, and consider whether the per-stage multiplier should be dampened (e.g., `0.3 * failed_stage_count.min(2)`) to prevent a single bad day from being catastrophic.","rationale":"The 3× amplification of both penalty and recovery rates is a significant behavioral change from the prior codebase. Without documentation or a cap, downstream integration tests may see different population dynamics. The old code's 0.3/0.35 constants were calibrated for single-resolution events."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"4edeb961-c3a3-4a25-a8fa-182208e04763"}
